# Killing-tensor search caches: resumable computation artifacts, not results.
# kt_def_rows_r3.pkl alone is 172 MB (above GitHub's limit) and is regenerable in ~24 min.
# They must stay on disk for power-cut resumption, and must NOT be versioned.
data/*.pkl
data/*.ckpt
# data/kt_*.out was ignored here until 2026-08-22. It should not have been. The rule above it
# targets the .pkl row-banks (2.6 GB, above GitHub's limit, regenerable); the .out RUN LOGS total
# 176 KB across 44 files and are the ONLY artifact carrying the numbers RESULTS 124 cites. A
# gitignore written for size swept up the receipts: every prover dimension in that section existed
# on one local disk and in no committed artifact. Found by running the bridge's provenance audit
# on ourselves after they ran it on themselves. The logs are now tracked.
data/s122_*.out
data/p0_*.out
